## Blank Values

Tooltips are not shown for the missing values `undefined`, `null` and `""` (empty string). To display a tooltip for a missing value, use a callback that returns non-empty content.

In the example below:

- The data has missing values `undefined`, `null` and `''` (empty String) as the first three rows.
- Column A uses `tooltip: true`, so no tooltip is shown for a missing displayed value.
- Column B uses a `tooltip` callback to return fallback content, so a tooltip is shown.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Blank Values" name="blank-values" /%}

## Tooltips for Truncated Text

Set `tooltipShowMode = 'whenTruncated'` to show tooltips only when the hovered or focused text is truncated.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltips" name="tooltip-show-mode" /%}

{% note %}
`tooltipShowMode = 'whenTruncated'` has no effect when using Browser Tooltips, as Browser Tooltips are controlled by the browser and not the grid.
{% /note %}

## Show and Hide Delay

By default, tooltips show after 2 seconds and have no timed hide. They stay open while their element or the tooltip is hovered, or their element has focus in a focus-enabled mode. Press `Escape` to dismiss them.

Set `tooltipHideDelay` to opt into a timeout. It does not close an interactive tooltip while keyboard focus is inside it.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltipShowDelay", "tooltipSwitchShowDelay", "tooltipHideDelay"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    tooltipShowDelay: 0,
    tooltipSwitchShowDelay: 1000,
    tooltipHideDelay: 2000,
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Show Hide Delay" name="show-hide-delay" /%}

{% note %}
Setting delays will have no effect if using Browser Tooltips as Browser Tooltips are controlled by the browser and not the grid.
{% /note %}

## Keyboard Focus

Set `tooltipTrigger: 'hoverOrFocus'` to show tooltips on both hover and keyboard focus. This applies wherever grid tooltips are supported, including cells, headers, menu items and tool panel items.

- `'hover'` (default): show on mouse hover only.
- `'focus'`: show on keyboard focus only, after `tooltipShowDelay`.
- `'hoverOrFocus'`: show on hover or keyboard focus after `tooltipShowDelay`.

In combined mode, the most recently hovered or focused element owns the tooltip. Moving away does not restore an earlier element's tooltip.

Tooltip text is available to screen readers immediately on focus, before the visual delay.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    tooltipTrigger: 'hoverOrFocus',
    tooltipShowDelay: 500,
    defaultColDef: {
        tooltip: true,
        headerTooltip: true,
    },
};
```

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltipTrigger", "getTooltipAriaDescription"] /%}

For custom tooltips with structured values, return plain text from `getTooltipAriaDescription`. Its `TooltipContentParams` contain the resolved tooltip `value`, without the component's `hideTooltipCallback`. Return `undefined` to use the resolved textual value, or `null` / `''` to omit the focus description. Browser Tooltips remain browser-controlled.

## Positioning

By default, tooltips are anchored to their target element (`tooltipAnchor: 'target'`) at `top-start`.

- `tooltipPosition` accepts `top`, `bottom`, `left` or `right`, each optionally suffixed with `-start` or `-end`. Start/end alignment follows text direction for top/bottom placements and means top/bottom for left/right placements.
- `tooltipAnchor: 'pointer'` anchors hover tooltips to the pointer. Focus tooltips always use the target element.
- `tooltipOffset` is the distance in pixels from the tooltip border (not the arrow tip) to the target or pointer. It defaults to `6`.

If the preferred side has insufficient space, the grid tries the opposite side, then uses whichever has more room. It shifts the tooltip to stay within the viewport and `popupParent`. If neither side fits, clamping can overlap the target. Use a larger `popupParent`, such as `document.body`, if more space is needed.

For per-source placement, provide a callback. `TooltipPositionParams` extends `TooltipCallbackParams` with `trigger` (`'hover'` or `'focus'`). Returning `undefined` uses the source's default placement.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    tooltipPosition: (params) => params.trigger === 'focus' ? 'bottom-start' : undefined,
};
```

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltipPosition", "tooltipAnchor", "tooltipOffset"] /%}

Change the controls below, then hover a cell or header, or focus it and navigate with the arrow keys. Press <kbd>Esc</kbd> to dismiss the tooltip without moving focus.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltip Positioning and Focus" name="tooltip-keyboard-focus" /%}

Use `postProcessPopup`'s `tooltipPosition` to inspect the resolved placement.

### Arrows

Built-in tooltips use their background and border for the arrow, including validation colours. Set the theme parameter `tooltipArrowSize` (default `5`) to `0` to hide it:

```js
const myTheme = themeQuartz.withParams({ tooltipArrowSize: 0 });
```

Custom components draw their own arrows, as shown below.

Centred placements point at the target's centre. Start/end placements point 12px inside that edge, or at the centre for small targets. Built-in arrows stay clear of the tooltip's rounded corners.

## Custom Component

The grid does not use the browser's default tooltip, instead it has a rich HTML Tooltip Component. The default Tooltip Component can be replaced with a Custom Tooltip Component using `colDef.tooltipComponent`.

`ITooltipParams<TData, TValue, TContext, TTooltipValue>` contains the resolved tooltip `value` and optional `hideTooltipCallback`. `TValue` describes column cells; the optional fourth generic describes a different tooltip payload and defaults to `TValue`. Tooltip component selectors receive arbitrary resolved content, which need not match the column's cell value type.

In the example below:

- `tooltipComponent` is set on the Default Column Definition so it applies to all Columns.
- `tooltipComponentParams` is set on the Athlete Column Definition to provide a Custom Property, in this instance setting the background colour.
- The component's CSS draws an arrow matching its background and clamps its offset to keep it clear of the corners.

Each tooltip element receives an `ag-tooltip-position-<position>` class for its resolved placement. `--ag-tooltip-arrow-offset` gives the physical distance to the arrow centre, measured from the **left** edge for top/bottom placements or the **top** edge for left/right placements, including in RTL. Use these in custom arrow CSS; placement is not passed to the component's params. Custom components must clamp the offset to suit their own dimensions, arrow size and corner radius.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Tooltip with Arrow" name="custom-tooltip-component" /%}

