## Interactive Tooltips

All tooltips can be hovered and their text selected. Use `tooltipInteraction: true`, or a callback for individual sources, to enable custom content containing inputs, buttons or links. Interactive tooltips use `role="dialog"` rather than `role="tooltip"`.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    // Only Athlete cell tooltips are interactive.
    tooltipInteraction: (params) =>
        params.location === 'cell' && params.column === params.api.getColumn('athlete')
}
```

The callback receives `TooltipCallbackParams` with the underlying source value and is evaluated each time a tooltip opens. It does not apply to Browser Tooltips.

For interactive tooltips:

- `Tab` from the source moves focus into the tooltip.
- `Escape` closes it and returns focus to the source if focus was inside.
- While focus is inside, hovering another element does not replace the tooltip.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltip Interaction" name="tooltip-interaction" /%}

The example below shows Tooltip Interaction with Custom Tooltips. Note the following:

- Tooltip is enabled for the Athlete and Age columns.
- The custom tooltip displays a text input and a Submit button which when clicked, updates the value of the `Athlete` Column cell in the hovered row and then closes itself by calling `hideTooltipCallback()`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Tooltip Interaction" name="custom-tooltip-interaction" /%}

## Row Groups

When a column is grouped, the generated group column inherits `tooltip`, `tooltipComponent`, and `tooltipComponentParams` from the underlying column's [Column Definition](./column-definitions/). This is consistent with how `valueFormatter` is inherited. With `groupDisplayType: 'multipleColumns'`, the group column header also inherits `headerTooltip`.

Cell tooltip properties set on `autoGroupColumnDef` (`tooltip` and `tooltipComponent`) apply to leaf rows only. `headerTooltip` still applies to the group column header.

In the example below:

- The Country and Year columns each define a `tooltip` callback. Hover a group key to see the tooltip inherited from the underlying column.
- `autoGroupColumnDef` defines a `tooltip` callback. Hover a leaf row in the group column to see it.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Group Tooltip" name="rowgroups-tooltip" /%}

{% note %}
`autoGroupColumnDef` cell tooltip properties apply to leaf rows only. Group rows inherit their cell tooltips from the underlying column `colDef`.
{% /note %}

### Grouped Column Headers

With `groupDisplayType: 'multipleColumns'`, each generated group column header inherits the `headerTooltip` from its underlying column `colDef`. Hover a group column header in the example below to see the inherited tooltip.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Grouped Column Header Tooltip" name="rowgroups-header-tooltip" /%}

### Full Width Group Rows

With `groupDisplayType: 'groupRows'`, full-width group rows inherit their tooltips from the underlying column `colDef`. Hover a group row in the example below to see the tooltip defined on the grouped column.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Full Width Group Row Tooltip" name="rowgroups-fullwidth-tooltip" /%}

### Aggregated Cells

When a group row displays an aggregated value in a data column, hovering that cell shows a tooltip for the aggregated value, not the underlying row data.

## Mouse Tracking

Set `tooltipMouseTrack: true` to anchor hover tooltips to the pointer and follow it as it moves, regardless of `tooltipAnchor`. Focus tooltips remain anchored to their target.

Pointer tracking updates, including `postProcessPopup` calls, are batched once per animation frame using the latest pointer position.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltip Mouse Tracking" name="tooltip-mouse-tracking" /%}

## Browser Tooltip

Set `enableBrowserTooltips: true` to use the browser's native tooltips instead of the grid's Tooltip Component.

Positioning, anchoring, offsets and arrow styling do not affect Browser Tooltips.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Default Browser Tooltip" name="default-tooltip" /%}

## Touch Devices

On iOS and Android, press and hold an element to show its tooltip immediately after the long press is recognised. Tap elsewhere to dismiss it.

- An available context menu or column menu takes precedence.
- Movement, cancellation or `suppressTouch: true` prevents the long-press tooltip.
- Browser Tooltips remain browser-controlled.
